<article class="env-lemma" id="0GKQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GKQ">Lemma <span data-tag="0GKQ">63.10.6</span>.</a> Let $f' : X' \to Y$ be a finite type separated morphism of quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes. Let $i : X \to X'$ be a thickening and denote $f = f' \circ i$. Let $\Lambda $ be a ring. For $K'$ in $D^+_{tors}(X'_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ or $K' \in D(X'_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ if $\Lambda $ is torsion, we have $Rf_!i^{-1}K' = Rf'_!K'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $i^{-1}$ and $i_* = i_!$ inverse equivalences of categories by the topological invariance of the small étale topos (Étale Cohomology, Theorem <a href="/tag/04DZ" data-tag="04DZ">59.45.2</a>) and we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0F7J" data-tag="0F7J">63.9.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>